WEBVTT


00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:06.439
The Silver Knit pattern controller is a
simple way to download stitch patterns to

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:09.170
your Silver/Studio
electronic knitting machine.

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:14.750
You can use the large, included stitch
library or create stitch patterns of your

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:17.900
own quickly using any
graphics design program.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:22.040
This tutorial goes beyond the
basics of using this device.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:27.110
For a quick overview of the basics, click
the arrow for a Knit it Now tutorial.

00:00:28.405 --> 00:00:32.935
Included in the utility software with
the controller are many stitch patterns.

00:00:33.715 --> 00:00:38.215
Look in your my documents, my
designs folder on your computer.

00:00:38.995 --> 00:00:43.495
The Silver Knit folder has samples of
many file formats that it supports.

00:00:44.515 --> 00:00:49.315
Included in the Silver Reed folder are
digitized stitch patterns based on Mylar

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:52.015
sheets used with the earlier machines.

00:00:58.115 --> 00:01:02.795
Click browse and open a stitch pattern
from the library or a pattern that you've

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:07.625
created, and you'll see a small preview of
the design with the stitches and rows and

00:01:07.625 --> 00:01:08.914
the knitting method shown.

00:01:09.664 --> 00:01:13.805
The Silver Knit uses three knitting
methods, zero one, two and three.

00:01:14.375 --> 00:01:18.785
It's based on the number of colors in your
design and it controls how the needles of

00:01:18.785 --> 00:01:20.914
your machine are selected as you knit.

00:01:22.870 --> 00:01:26.600
Once you've selected your pattern, it's
time to download it to the Silver Knit

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:27.400
controller.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:29.260
This is where the fun starts.

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:31.720
You can customize your
stitch pattern here.

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:34.330
First, select your machine

00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:44.480
The top section of this page is where you
can quickly modify your stitch pattern,

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:48.860
make it double wide,
reversing it, mirror it.

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:50.960
There's lots of options here.

00:01:52.430 --> 00:01:56.990
in the sections below, you can control
the position of your stitch pattern for

00:01:56.990 --> 00:01:59.690
isolated motifs and much, much more.

00:02:03.475 --> 00:02:05.635
Let's use a little duck
pattern and play a bit.

00:02:05.965 --> 00:02:07.465
Click the download button.

00:02:10.065 --> 00:02:14.175
Now we'll use the upside down function,
but you can try any of the various

00:02:14.175 --> 00:02:15.885
features and see what they do.

00:02:16.635 --> 00:02:19.035
Tick the checkbox and click okay.

00:02:24.475 --> 00:02:27.475
The new information will
download to the controller.

00:02:28.109 --> 00:02:36.280
Click okay again, and we'll use the knit
button to preview our changes and there he

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:36.489
is.

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:39.400
Ducky is standing on his head.

00:02:45.370 --> 00:02:50.109
Other options on the download screen
includes starting with the carriage on the

00:02:50.109 --> 00:02:50.890
left.

00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:58.220
You can control the needle
selection for easier seaming.

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:04.750
You can enter the pattern width.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:09.630
This is not, may or may not be the
knitting with just the stitch pattern

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:10.210
width

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:15.990
you can position the design
on your knitted piece.

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:25.190
And you can also select a portion
of the stitch pattern to use.

00:03:34.505 --> 00:03:38.315
For this example, we're going to
center our duck over 25 stitches.

00:03:39.335 --> 00:03:43.745
We also want the pattern shifted over
a bit to be off center on the garment.

00:03:45.005 --> 00:03:50.165
When we download and preview our duck
with these settings, you'll see that the

00:03:50.165 --> 00:03:53.165
pattern controller followed
our instructions perfectly.

00:03:54.060 --> 00:04:00.450
We have a margin on the left and our
duck is centered over the 25 stitches.

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:13.030
Notice that at the bottom of the
interactive knitting screen are shown the

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:17.769
stitches and rows in our design,
as well as the point cam positions.

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:22.180
It also includes a
contrasting color indicator.

00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:30.770
For our next example.

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:34.099
We only want to use the flowers
at the bottom of this design.

00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:40.159
We've already opened the bear pattern and
we've been downloaded the entire thing one

00:04:40.159 --> 00:04:40.670
time.

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:46.849
We'll use the knit button again
to preview the design close up.

00:04:48.225 --> 00:04:53.115
And you'll see that we only want those
first eight rows row one through eight of

00:04:53.115 --> 00:04:55.815
the pattern for our new design.

00:04:57.735 --> 00:05:02.055
Now close the knit screen and we'll
click the download button again.

00:05:08.305 --> 00:05:14.424
On the downloads screen, we will edit the
pattern indicators section and tell the

00:05:14.424 --> 00:05:17.155
Silver Knit utility what
rows we want to use.

00:05:18.354 --> 00:05:19.315
Click okay.

00:05:19.344 --> 00:05:20.515
Click okay.

00:05:20.695 --> 00:05:26.905
Click knit to preview and you'll see that
it's chosen the eight rows of flowers that

00:05:26.905 --> 00:05:29.935
we want, and these will transfer
to our knitting machine.

00:05:32.635 --> 00:05:37.425
The Silver Knit pattern controller is
a great option for silver or a singer.

00:05:37.435 --> 00:05:38.125
Knitters.

00:05:39.295 --> 00:05:43.135
Check the Knit it Now learning
library for even more tutorials.

